(Voltage bias controls:) {/Helvetica-Bold cf} 2 16 0.000 1.000 -448 1184 label

(together in the harness chip, so the inactive output should be disabled along with its corresponding bias current.) 
{CR} 
(drive output for lower voltages or if the user project does not draw current through that signal line.  The two outputs are connected) 
{CR} 
(draws current from that line.  The voltage bias generator can supply over 100uA of current with the high drive output.  Use the low) 
{CR} 
(The high power/high drive should be used if higher voltage outputs are being used \(around 2.5V or higher\), or if the user project) 
